extends RefCounted

const TOPICS := [
	["Deployment", "Select a sector and difficulty at Deploy. Act I ends at the miniboss, then the Act II gate opens. Defeat the guardian in Act II, open the boss cache and reach the extraction pad to bank the rewards.", "Clear a sector on Normal to unlock Hard there and improve your odds of rare loot. Clear every sector on Hard to unlock Expert. In co-op, every operator needs the difficulty unlocked. The NOVA Archive shows a sector's loot after your first clear."],
	["Movement & traversal", "Hold jump for more height. Use an air dash near the top of the jump to cross long gaps. Hold toward a wall while airborne to slide down it, then jump off and steer back to climb. Press up as you reach ladders or vines to grab them.", "On a drop-through deck, hold crouch and press Drop. When you slide underneath low clearance, RX-07 stays low until there's room to stand. Brake early on frosted decking. Check the binding pages in Settings for your controls."],
	["Buster, saber & suits", "Tap Buster for one shot. In the Standard Frame, hold and release Buster to pierce raised purple shields. Tap Sword in rhythm for a combo or hold and release in the Standard Frame for a ranged slice.", "Defeating a guardian unlocks its suit for the current run. Cycle suits with the shoulder buttons or your swap controls. Press Suit Weapon to spend energy on the equipped suit's attack. Regular Buster shots are available in every suit."],
	["Checkpoints & reconstruction", "Touch a checkpoint to set your return point. A death uses a life. Run out of lives and NOVA reconstructs you at the station. You can deploy to any previously unlocked sector.", "Reconstruction resets your Operator Level and run suits and clears your equipped gear and quick slots. Your Player Level, stored items, banked currency, learned recipes and permanent enhancements carry over."],
	["Shop & currency", "Spend Bolts at the Shop on recovery supplies, buffs and crafting materials. Better stock unlocks at Operator Level milestones. To stow purchases, open Equipment → Storage and select a stack in Inventory.", "Boss clears and challenges reward Core Shards. Spend them on permanent talents in Core Ascension, in the Workshop."],
	["Core Ascension", "Spend Core Shards in Survivability, Damage or Scavenger. Install one talent in each earlier tier to advance in that branch. Every talent has three ranks. Tier 5 introduces a capstone at Player Level 28 that can reach Rank III at Player Level 50.", "Field Reboot lets you revive one downed ally per boss attempt. Get close to the ally marker and press Field Interact, then stay close and avoid damage until the reboot finishes. Higher ranks restore more HP."],
	["Foundry routes", "The Kiln Warden awards one run module of your choice. In Act II, step on the lower gallery's pressure plate to release the return shutter, and break the cracked wall to open the route. The rolling slag boulder takes ten regular Buster hits or four charged hits. Shoot it from outside the chute.", "The upper gantry and low cooling tunnel offer different loot. On Expert, shoot the lit relief valve after the Forge Titan's rupture charge to vent the flames and expose his core."],
	["Blueprint hunts", "After your first clear, visit the NOVA Archive and pin a blueprint from that sector's boss cache. Deploy shows the source, minimum difficulty, required Operator Level and progress.", "Three eligible extractions earn the pinned blueprint if it hasn't dropped. Your hunt progress stays with the operator when saved."],
	["Equipment & Storage", "In Gear, choose a socket to see compatible items. Equip one item per socket and check the operator's stats. In Storage, select a stack on the left to move it to the right.", "Salvage recovered in a mission goes to Storage when you extract. Equipped gear stays at risk on a run."],
	["Quick slots", "Assign a supply to a D-pad direction from Equipment or the mission pause inventory. Each direction holds one item type, up to three of that item. The upper limit for an inventory stack is 100.", "Press a direction during gameplay to use one supply. Health and energy supplies only consume when there is something to restore. Recovery items and temporary buffs are described on their item cards."],
	["Blueprints & Crafting", "Select a blueprint in Storage and confirm Learn Blueprint. In the Workshop, review the cost and choose Craft & Equip or Craft to Storage. Equipping sends the old gear to Storage.", "Boss caches guarantee a blueprint and can also contain materials and supplies."],
	["Social & co-op", "Use Social to add friends and accept invites. Start a Group from Deploy. The leader selects the sector and starts the mission. Press Enter in the station or in the field to chat with the whole party or reply to a whisper.", "Teammate health appears beneath your own HUD. Loot, lives and inventories are personal. The party shares kill XP and boss suit unlocks. Everyone still in the fight needs to cross the boss door before it closes."],
	["Operator and Profile XP", "Defeating enemies and bosses earns Operator XP. Leveling up raises your stats and restores half of your new maximum HP, up to full health. NOVA resets Operator Level when reconstructing you after a failed run.", "Extract from both acts of a sector to earn permanent Player Profile XP. Visit the Profile station for your fastest extractions, clear count and longest surviving Operator."],
	["Voice chat", "Open Settings → Audio to enable party voice and select your input and output devices. Use Test Microphone to check the meter and hear your recording through the selected output.", "Bind Push to Talk under Keyboard & Mouse or Controller. The mic beside a party member lights up while their voice is coming through."],
	["Challenges", "Each unlocked sector has five challenges. Requirements can include reaching Act II, extracting at high health, moving quickly or gathering salvage.", "Every set resets at local midnight, even when the game is closed. The challenge panel shows the time left and the bonus Core Shards for completing all five."],
	["System & Save", "Use the System pad to save your operator manually. Operator slots are managed from the title screen. A save includes banked progress and the current deployment when available.", "Settings covers audio, video, gameplay, keyboard and controller bindings, and installed game updates. Toggle first-time hub tips in Gameplay. This manual remains available either way."],
]
